# Castle Garenbrig's six {G} pay for an ability of a creature as the ability was activated (CR 602.2a, 113.7a): a source
# that leaves the battlefield while the cost is paid is still the creature whose ability it is. (A regression check: a
# sacrificed object's last-known characteristics say the same, so this holds whichever way the source is read; the
# scenario of March of the Machines leaving tells the two apart.)
# Turn 3 Bot1 activates Basking Rootwalla's "{1}{G}: +2/+2" with nothing in the pool. While paying (CR 601.2g) it sacrifices
# the Rootwalla to Phyrexian Altar for {G}, then activates the Castle, paying {2}{G}{G} with that {G}, the Forest, Mox
# Emerald and Mox Jet. Two of the six {G} pay the Rootwalla's {1}{G}, though the Rootwalla is in the graveyard by then: four
# are left, and the ability resolves and does nothing.

